cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Code and data for: Print the trivial arm: three scales at which a do-nothing baseline decided what an image restoration comparison could conclude
message: If you use this code or data, please cite this archive and the manuscript.
type: dataset
authors:
  - given-names: Zeyu
    family-names: Fu
    email: fuzeyu99@126.com
    orcid: 'https://orcid.org/0009-0001-8329-0108'
    affiliation: 'Army Medical University, Chongqing, China'
abstract: >-
  Toy training records, per-crop fidelity tables for a released restoration model and two interpolations, inference manifests, a memory-ceiling skip census, figure code and manuscript source for a study showing that at three scales of one restoration project the untouched input or the cheapest interpolation determined what the comparison could conclude.
keywords:
  - image restoration
  - super-resolution
  - baselines
  - perception-distortion tradeoff
  - evaluation
  - selection effect
  - negative result
